 "notes": "Strip d: x 4920-6320 plus ~300 px overlap (picks from x 4659 to 6650). Plate 22-66 is roughly north-up. Street centres taken midway between the block (lot) lines; house numbers sit inside the street band. Harvey Avenue (x~5120-5140) runs south from the plate edge, crosses Union, then S-curves west at y~2850-2950 and continues south as Vernon Place (x~4880-4895) to Oak Street; the name change point is not printed, only 'HARVEY' north of the curve and 'VERNON'/'PL.' south of it. Melish Avenue jogs at Harvey (west part y~2378, east part y~2445) and again at Reading (y~2442 west, ~2495 east). Union Street jogs ~40 px at Reading. Winslow Avenue: printed '...AVENUE' between Lincoln and Tennis Lane and 'WINSLOW' between Crown and McMillan; treated as one street (x~6400-6450). Oak Street west of Reading is printed only 'ST.'; named Oak from continuous house numbering. 'Bowman' (no suffix) and 'Arndt' (no suffix) recorded as printed. Bottom street is East McMillan Street (printed 'E. McMILLAN STREET' west and east of this strip); its south side is the plate edge, with stubs of streets running south off the plate, named '?' with their printed fragments in notes. Big spaced names across lots (CARPENTER, WALKER?, H. WAHKING HEIRS, J. FRAHER, N.S. WADE'S, THOS. McGECHIN'S, VERNONVILLE) are owner/subdivision names, not streets. The diagonal tinted line from (5600,2900) to (5450,3650) is a property line, not a street. A scan fold runs vertically near x 5200-5240 in the lower half."
}